<header class="ref-head yr-head"><p class="cty-kicker">Year by year · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p><h1 class="research-title">1806</h1><p class="ref-lede">1806 in world history: 36 events, 12 births, 13 deaths, 18 states founded and 26 that came to an end. 1,158 recorded states existed that year.</p></header>
<nav class="ref-letters yr-near" aria-label="Nearby years"><a href="/years/1802">1802</a><a href="/years/1803">1803</a><a href="/years/1804">1804</a><a href="/years/1805">1805</a><a href="/years/1806" aria-current="page">1806</a><a href="/years/1807">1807</a><a href="/years/1808">1808</a><a href="/years/1809">1809</a><a href="/years/1810">1810</a></nav>
<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/london" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/london.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/january-9">9 January</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Admiral Nelson is buried in St Paul's Cathedral</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">After a vast procession through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/horatio-nelson">Horatio Nelson</a> was laid to rest in the crypt of St Paul's. He had been killed at his victory at Trafalgar the previous October.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/thomas-jefferson" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thomas-jefferson.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/march-29">29 March</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Thomas Jefferson authorises the Cumberland Road</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Jefferson signed the act for a road from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cumberland">Cumberland</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maryland">Maryland</a>, to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ohio">Ohio</a>, the first great federally financed highway of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>. By 1839 the National Road reached Vandalia, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/illinois">Illinois</a>, 591 miles from Cumberland.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/united-states">United States</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thomas-jefferson">Thomas Jefferson</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/charlemagne" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/charlemagne.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/august-6">6 August</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Francis II dissolves the Holy Roman Empire</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Under pressure from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francis-ii">Francis II</a> laid down the imperial crown and dissolved the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a>. A political order dating back to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charlemagne">Charlemagne</a>'s coronation in 800 came to an end.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charlemagne">Charlemagne</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francis-ii">Francis II</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-jena-auerstedt" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-jena-auerstedt.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/october-27">27 October</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Napoleon enters Berlin after the Prussian defeat at Jena–Auerstedt</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a> entered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berlin">Berlin</a> without a fight, three days after French forces had captured the Prussian capital following their victory at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jena">Jena</a>–Auerstedt. From the city he later issued the Berlin Decree implementing his <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/continental-system">Continental System</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-jena-auerstedt">Battle of Jena–Auerstedt</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-blaauwberg" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-blaauwberg.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-blaauwberg">Battle of Blaauwberg</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Blaauwberg was fought on 8 January 1806 near Cape Town, when a British force under General David Baird defeated the Batavian garrison of Governor Jan Willem Janssens.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-misar" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-misar.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-misar">Battle of Mišar</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Mišar was fought in August 1806 near Šabac in western Serbia, where Serbian rebels under Karađorđe defeated a larger Ottoman army from Bosnia.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Treaty</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/rhine-confederation-act">Rhine Confederation Act</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Rhine Confederation Act was a treaty signed in Paris on 12 July 1806 by sixteen German states, including Bavaria, Württemberg and Baden, which left the Holy Roman Empire and formed the Confederation of the Rhine under Napoleon's protection.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/dissolution-of-the-holy-roman-empire">Dissolution of the Holy Roman Empire</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The dissolution of the Holy Roman Empire took place in 1806, when Emperor Francis II abdicated the imperial title following Napoleon's victories and the creation of the Confederation of the Rhine.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Treaty · Peace</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-posen">Treaty of Posen</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Treaty of Posen, signed on 11 December 1806 at Posen (Poznań), made peace between Napoleon and Elector Frederick Augustus III of Saxony, who had fought on the Prussian side at Jena.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Treaty</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/anglo-sikh-treaty-of-1806">Anglo-Sikh Treaty of 1806</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Anglo-Sikh Treaty of 1806 was an agreement between Ranjit Singh and the British East India Company.</p></div></li></ol></section>
