 Jena–Auerstedt</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Prussia declares war and Napoleon sends 180,000 men through the Franconian Forest towards Saxony and Berlin</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-jena-auerstedt"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Jena%E2%80%93Auerstedt.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Jena–Auerstedt</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Napoleon defeats Hohenlohe's Prussians near Jena</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-jena-auerstedt"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Jena%E2%80%93Auerstedt.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Jena–Auerstedt</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Davout's III Corps defeats the main Prussian army at Auerstedt, where the Duke of Brunswick is mortally wounded</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-jena-auerstedt"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Jena%E2%80%93Auerstedt.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Jena–Auerstedt</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">A large body of Prussian troops surrenders in the Capitulation of Erfurt</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-jena-auerstedt"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Jena%E2%80%93Auerstedt.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Jena–Auerstedt</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Davout leads his III Corps into Berlin</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-jena-auerstedt"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Jena%E2%80%93Auerstedt.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Jena–Auerstedt</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Hohenlohe's force surrenders after the Battle of Prenzlau</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-jena-auerstedt"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Jena%E2%80%93Auerstedt.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Jena–Auerstedt</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Blücher's corps is surrounded at Lübeck and surrenders the next day</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/battle/battle-of-jena-auerstedt"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Battle%20of%20Jena%E2%80%93Auerstedt.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Battle of Jena–Auerstedt</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The siege of Magdeburg ends with Ney's capture of the fortress</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/cape-town"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Cape%20Town.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Cape Town</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">British forces take the Cape after the Battle of Blaauwberg</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/benito-juarez"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Benito%20Ju%C3%A1rez.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Benito Juárez</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Benito Juárez is born in San Pablo Guelatao, Oaxaca, to Zapotec peasants</span></li></ul></section>
